  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable and accessible fish for all</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims at improving the aquaculture sector in Myanmar through the establishment of a more profitable inclusive farming model that adds more value to local communities and to stakeholders across the supply chain.Through the improvement of quality and access of inputs such as seeds and feed, together with upgrading the technical knowledge and know-how of farmers, academic institutions and technical support staff from both private and public organisations.At the same time the farming systems are developed into more efficient systems towards more productive, shorter cycle and more diverse species, and increased transfer of adapted technologies.Finally, promotion of the products towards consumers and new markets is an active component within the project. This will result in improved access to markets for over 15,000 farmers and an increase of income for 45,000 individuals, of which 20% are female.</narrative>
  </description>
